diff --git a/openspec/specs/search-filters/spec.md b/openspec/specs/search-filters/spec.md
index ce84761..779cf3f 100644
--- a/openspec/specs/search-filters/spec.md
+++ b/openspec/specs/search-filters/spec.md
@@ -32,3 +32,41 @@ The system SHALL provide a sort control on the search page that allows the user
 - **WHEN** the user changes sort and navigates to a book detail page and back
 - **THEN** the sort control SHALL still show the previously selected sort option
 - **THEN** the results SHALL be served from cache (no new network request)
+
+---
+
+### Requirement: User can filter search results by author
+
+The system SHALL provide an author control on the search page once results are
+available. The control SHALL be a `<select>` with the accessible label
+"Author:" and the id `author-select`. Its options SHALL be "All authors"
+(empty value) followed by the deduplicated author names present in the current
+results. Selecting an author SHALL re-fetch results from the Open Library
+search API with the `author` query parameter set to that author, reset
+pagination to the first page, and display only books by the selected author.
+Selecting "All authors" SHALL clear the filter and restore the unfiltered
+results.
+
+#### Scenario: Author options reflect current results
+
+- **WHEN** a search returns results from authors
+- **THEN** the author control SHALL list "All authors" plus each distinct author name once
+- **THEN** the selected option SHALL default to "All authors"
+
+#### Scenario: User selects an author
+
+- **WHEN** the user selects an author from the author control
+- **THEN** the system SHALL request search results with `author=<selected author>`
+- **THEN** pagination SHALL reset to the first page
+- **THEN** the results grid SHALL only contain books by the selected author
+
+#### Scenario: User clears the author filter
+
+- **WHEN** the user selects "All authors"
+- **THEN** the system SHALL request results without an `author` parameter
+- **THEN** the unfiltered results SHALL be displayed again
+
+#### Scenario: Author control only visible with results
+
+- **WHEN** there are no results (empty state, error, or no query)
+- **THEN** the author control SHALL NOT be visible
